// Types Of Containers :
/*
1. Sequence Containers --> stores data in liner fashion , ie. Array , Vector , List , Dequeue etc . 
2. Associative Containers --> stores data in tree like structure , provide direact access to data , ie. set , multiset , map etc .
3. Derived Containers --> (Provide Real world modling) , ie. stack , queue , priority-queue etc. 

-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Sequence Container :
A. Vector =>
Random Access : Fast !
Insertion / Delition : Slow !
Delition at the end : Fast !
B. List (Linked List) =>
Random Access : Slow !
Insertion / Delition in middle : Fast !
Insertion / Delition at the end : Fast !

2. Associative Containers : All Operation Fast Except Random Access !

3. Derived Containers : Depends !
*/